# Pitch Deck end-scope SoT

Canonical: `local/schema-driven-deck-generation-engine/END-SCOPE-SOT.md` (sales-mcp) or `local/pitch-deck-mvp/` (IsItInProd copy).  
Historical Prodie ideation spec (not runtime contract): `docs/PRODIE-IDEATION-SPEC.md`.  
Living goal/progress: `PROGRESS.md`.

Product specs: Pitch Deck Workflow + Fortune Logic Guide V1. Assets: `FortuneAI_DeckTemplate.pptx`, `Fortune_AITool_GTM_Database`, Inventory Calendar.

## End state (MVP)

Upstream (**Pitch Deck Builder**, **Sales HQ**, or any caller) sends a **complete `DeckSchema` payload** — Discovery fields + `confirmed_products[]` (`name`, `category`, `price`, `cadence`) → **sales-mcp `build_deck`** (validate + C1 FortuneAI assembly + exact Deck Path/Slide # clones + C2 fills [+ optional QA rail]) → PPTX.

**sales-mcp is deck generation only.** It does not ideate, propose a menu, or choose products.  
**The caller owns product lock upstream.** Humans vet **product names**, not Hunter slide numbers. After lock, A5 maps name/category → clone.

**Prodie is not the ideation brain on this MCP.** If Prodie appears at all, it is a transport/client forwarding an already-locked payload — not proposing or checkboxing products here.

**`confirm_mix` is optional legacy** — validates name+category and hydrates prices from GTM when the caller omits full products. Not the primary associate path.

Guide Media Mix auto-fund is **not** required MVP.

## Not end state

Titan/RAG product matching · MCP `LogicGuideEngine` as associate runtime · Prodie ideating/proposing through this MCP · Cursor stylist MVP (PI-2754) · `Category_Presentation_*` spine · AI rewriting product slides · `propose_mix` MCP tool.

## Progress (2026-09-09)

- Done: A1–A3, C3 schema, A5 exact map, C1 FortuneAI assembly, C2 placeholders, I1 data, optional I3 `confirm_mix`
- Remaining out-of-repo: Pitch Deck Builder UI / upstream product lock (PI-2350)

## Hard rules

1. Missing GTM row / inventory hold / price mismatch → fail loud; never silent substitute.
2. Conference Sponsorship → GTM escalate; do not invent conference slides.
3. C2 fills named FortuneAI slots only; never rewrite A5 product clones.
4. Merge A5 before Titan cleanup; don’t delete RAG in the C2 PR.
5. Primary path: `build_deck(full DeckSchema)` — never search Hunter decks for substitute product slides.
6. Do not default-check sold/held inventory lines (upstream responsibility).
